1
00:00:01,101 --> 00:00:03,069
It's a top-secret hospitalization,
so be careful.

2
00:00:04,637 --> 00:00:08,141
We're the only ones who know
about this secret VIP.

3
00:00:08,241 --> 00:00:10,443
To keep other patients
and employees from noticing,

4
00:00:10,677 --> 00:00:13,847
I think we need to use a fake name
on the room and bed tag.

5
00:00:13,913 --> 00:00:15,315
Really?

6
00:00:15,448 --> 00:00:18,118
So, Yuji Kudo isn't his stage name?

7
00:00:18,184 --> 00:00:19,185
It's his real name.

8
00:00:19,285 --> 00:00:22,522
Yu has been living true
to himself since his debut.

9
00:00:22,822 --> 00:00:25,925
Since I was in high school,
to me, Yu has been

10
00:00:28,995 --> 00:00:29,963
a god!

11
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:32,198
Hey, are you listening? He's a legend!

12
00:00:32,265 --> 00:00:35,168
- It's about time for him to arrive.
- All right!

13
00:00:36,269 --> 00:00:39,272
- You scared me!
- Do you want me to operate on that VIP?

14
00:00:39,406 --> 00:00:41,508
Why the heck are you here?
It's none of your business!

15
00:00:41,608 --> 00:00:43,610
The VIP asked for Dr. Yuzuru Hara himself!

16
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:45,812
- My name's "Mamoru."
- "Mamoru"?

17
00:00:45,879 --> 00:00:49,482
It wouldn't be an overstatement to
say I became a surgeon for this day.

18
00:00:51,584 --> 00:00:54,087
- What are you looking at?
- I can't help it.

19
00:00:54,154 --> 00:00:56,122
Kin's hairstyle is funny.

20
00:00:56,189 --> 00:00:59,659
<i>This is the story of
a maverick female doctor.</i>

21
00:01:00,593 --> 00:01:02,962
He sure is late. When is he coming?

22
00:01:03,530 --> 00:01:05,465
Isn't that him?

23
00:01:07,934 --> 00:01:09,369
That's not him at all.

24
00:01:09,436 --> 00:01:11,104
- Oh, dear.
- What?

25
00:01:11,171 --> 00:01:12,806
NO PARKING

26
00:01:12,872 --> 00:01:14,908
Out of the way! Mr. Niizu!

27
00:01:16,209 --> 00:01:17,677
I've been expecting you.

28
00:01:18,211 --> 00:01:19,312
Come this way.

29
00:01:19,712 --> 00:01:20,680
Out of the way!

30
00:01:24,084 --> 00:01:27,821
Niizu? Is that the Internet
breakout singer-songwriter?

31
00:01:27,954 --> 00:01:29,889
Compared to Yu, that guy's a small fry.

32
00:01:30,090 --> 00:01:32,759
- Don't call him a small fry. Wow!
- He sure is late!

33
00:01:32,992 --> 00:01:35,929
- Isn't that Yu?
- Yu!

34
00:01:35,995 --> 00:01:39,032
Dr. Kaji! He's here! Yu!

35
00:01:52,979 --> 00:01:57,350
Yu, I run an <i>oden</i> stand over there.
Come eat there!

36
00:01:58,118 --> 00:01:59,352
Sure thing.

37
00:02:00,353 --> 00:02:03,790
Yu!

38
00:02:08,661 --> 00:02:09,963
Settle down!

39
00:02:10,330 --> 00:02:11,865
I'm Kudo. Nice to meet you.

40
00:02:12,465 --> 00:02:13,666
We've been expecting you.

41
00:02:13,967 --> 00:02:15,835
I'm Dr. Kaji, director of Next-Generation

42
00:02:15,902 --> 00:02:17,203
Ultra-Minimally Invasive Surgery.

43
00:02:17,971 --> 00:02:19,005
Nice to meet you.

44
00:02:19,072 --> 00:02:21,141
YUJI

45
00:02:21,541 --> 00:02:24,344
- Nice to meet you. I'm Mamoru Hara.
- Speak up.

46
00:02:24,477 --> 00:02:26,646
- Are you Dr. Hara?
- Yes.

47
00:02:27,147 --> 00:02:28,481
Nice to meet you.

48
00:02:32,085 --> 00:02:33,953
Yu, give me your autograph!

49
00:02:36,756 --> 00:02:38,758
- I don't care if I die now.
- You're making me sick.

50
00:02:39,092 --> 00:02:41,928
And what the heck happened
to this being top secret?

51
00:02:42,962 --> 00:02:46,766
My husband is always changing his mind.

52
00:02:47,233 --> 00:02:51,671
He said, "Sneaking in the back door
to the hospital is totally not rocking."

53
00:02:51,771 --> 00:02:55,675
We live separately,
but I am still his wife.

54
00:02:56,476 --> 00:03:00,847
<i>In 2019, the ivory towers are
completely crumbling.</i>

55
00:03:00,980 --> 00:03:03,149
What? Takuya Niizu?

56
00:03:03,750 --> 00:03:05,985
He's a popular artist?

57
00:03:06,386 --> 00:03:09,355
His debut song has been viewed
more than 900 million times.

58
00:03:09,422 --> 00:03:11,090
Oh, is that right? Wow!

59
00:03:11,157 --> 00:03:15,862
We need to be particularly careful
when entertainers are hospitalized.

60
00:03:15,995 --> 00:03:17,964
- Yes, sir.
- If he's cured,

61
00:03:18,064 --> 00:03:21,467
it has fabulous PR effects at zero cost.

62
00:03:21,901 --> 00:03:25,672
So has the rock star I asked here arrived?

63
00:03:25,772 --> 00:03:29,342
Just now, he made a flamboyant
appearance at the front entrance.

64
00:03:29,809 --> 00:03:32,111
- That's magnificent.
- What rock star?

65
00:03:33,146 --> 00:03:34,647
Yuji Kudo.

66
00:03:37,884 --> 00:03:39,552
- I'm sorry.
- Are you okay?

67
00:03:39,986 --> 00:03:41,888
Thank you. Sorry about that.

68
00:03:42,689 --> 00:03:46,926
Dr. Ushio and Dr. Hamachi,
just for good measure,

69
00:03:47,126 --> 00:03:49,128
I've looked into your affairs.

70
00:03:50,530 --> 00:03:53,233
Let me give this to you
right here and now.

71
00:03:53,833 --> 00:03:56,769
That Tange Nicholas who's in detention,

72
00:03:57,437 --> 00:04:01,841
it's quite likely
that he won't be coming back.

73
00:04:03,676 --> 00:04:07,113
You short sold one million shares of

74
00:04:07,513 --> 00:04:09,282
Hexagon Bridge

75
00:04:09,649 --> 00:04:12,085
then manipulated the stock
by leaking on the Internet

76
00:04:12,151 --> 00:04:14,287
that President Rokkakubashi
was sick with cancer.

77
00:04:14,587 --> 00:04:18,791
As a result, you reaped
immense profits. Isn't that right?

78
00:04:21,227 --> 00:04:23,763
That's outright insider trading!

79
00:04:25,331 --> 00:04:29,802
Though Tange Nicholas scouted
the both of you and hired you,

80
00:04:30,403 --> 00:04:35,808
to me, you're valuable subordinates.
You're treasures. You're assets.

81
00:04:35,942 --> 00:04:37,810
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

82
00:04:37,944 --> 00:04:43,750
If you two would work
for me and be my brains,

83
00:04:43,850 --> 00:04:45,551
I would be very grateful.

84
00:04:46,319 --> 00:04:47,353
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

85
00:04:49,222 --> 00:04:53,192
<i>It's one-of-a-kind</i>

86
00:04:53,459 --> 00:04:57,864
<i>We're unrivaled</i>

87
00:04:57,964 --> 00:04:59,999
<i>No strong wind can...</i>

88
00:05:00,099 --> 00:05:03,803
<i>Japan's university hospitals have
fallen into tremendous debt.</i>

89
00:05:03,870 --> 00:05:06,172
<i>Lifesaving medical treatment</i>

90
00:05:06,239 --> 00:05:10,643
<i>has entered the era of
financial jungle law.</i>

91
00:05:11,210 --> 00:05:15,648
<i>Meanwhile, this freelance maverick doctor,
who was never part of</i>

92
00:05:16,049 --> 00:05:19,752
<i>a university medical department,
showed up.</i>

93
00:05:20,620 --> 00:05:21,954
This way, Mr. Kudo.

94
00:05:23,990 --> 00:05:26,292
<i>This woman hates groups,</i>

95
00:05:26,426 --> 00:05:30,530
<i>authority, and restrictions.</i>

96
00:05:30,963 --> 00:05:34,233
<i>Her specialized medical license
and well-honed skills</i>

97
00:05:34,534 --> 00:05:35,802
<i>are her weapons.</i>

98
00:05:37,036 --> 00:05:38,705
Mr. Kudo is coming through.

99
00:05:38,805 --> 00:05:41,140
- Nice to meet you.
- Who are you, pal?

100
00:05:41,207 --> 00:05:43,509
You don't know? I'm sorry, Mr. Kudo.

101
00:05:43,609 --> 00:05:47,547
- Kudo? Who's that?
- Yuji Kudo!

102
00:05:47,613 --> 00:05:49,349
- You really don't know me?
- Not at all.

103
00:05:49,415 --> 00:05:51,918
There's actually a Japanese person
who doesn't know me?

104
00:05:51,984 --> 00:05:55,555
That must mean all you did
was study medicine in university.

105
00:05:56,889 --> 00:05:58,291
It's nice to know you.

106
00:05:58,558 --> 00:06:00,526
If I'm operating on you,
it's good to know you.

107
00:06:00,593 --> 00:06:02,595
I'm good and fast.

108
00:06:02,662 --> 00:06:04,731
I like it. You've got tons of confidence.

109
00:06:05,031 --> 00:06:07,467
That's just like me.
You're the female Yuji Kudo.

110
00:06:07,567 --> 00:06:09,168
I'm Michiko Daimon.

111
00:06:09,769 --> 00:06:13,072
I'm very sorry about this.
Let me show you to the VIP room.

112
00:06:19,912 --> 00:06:22,782
Oh, he just has hemorrhoids.

113
00:06:22,882 --> 00:06:25,251
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

114
00:06:25,451 --> 00:06:28,888
<i>otherwise known as Doctor X.</i>

115
00:06:52,912 --> 00:06:53,780
Here you go.

116
00:06:57,850 --> 00:06:59,819
This is the VIP room?

117
00:07:01,187 --> 00:07:04,590
It's smaller than my own bathroom.

118
00:07:04,824 --> 00:07:08,327
Their VIP room was already taken.

119
00:07:08,428 --> 00:07:10,530
They said this was the only one open.

120
00:07:10,863 --> 00:07:12,165
I'm terribly sorry!

121
00:07:13,099 --> 00:07:14,200
You just missed getting it.

122
00:07:14,267 --> 00:07:17,837
Who's a more important patient
than Yuji Kudo?

123
00:07:18,104 --> 00:07:19,806
The prime minister?

124
00:07:19,906 --> 00:07:21,908
- Well, actually...
- Yu!

125
00:07:21,974 --> 00:07:23,609
I really am terribly sorry!

126
00:07:24,477 --> 00:07:27,680
I don't mind,

127
00:07:27,914 --> 00:07:31,484
but what would Yuji Kudo say?

128
00:07:34,387 --> 00:07:35,822
Excuse me.

129
00:07:36,589 --> 00:07:38,191
NURSE
KANA IINO

130
00:07:38,257 --> 00:07:39,725
Mr. Kudo, time for your endoscope exam.

131
00:07:39,792 --> 00:07:40,626
Come with me.

132
00:07:41,260 --> 00:07:43,029
PROCTOLOGY

133
00:07:47,033 --> 00:07:48,301
Is that you, Niizu?

134
00:07:50,102 --> 00:07:53,272
Oh, Mr. Kudo. Hello. Thanks for
your help at the summer festival.

135
00:07:53,406 --> 00:07:56,008
You doing well? Oh, I guess you're not.

136
00:07:56,209 --> 00:07:58,010
This is a hospital, after all.

137
00:07:59,545 --> 00:08:01,047
Are you seeing the proctologist too?

138
00:08:01,948 --> 00:08:04,951
Let's both get operated on fast
and get better, okay?

139
00:08:05,117 --> 00:08:06,919
Take care of yourself too, sir.

140
00:08:12,425 --> 00:08:17,430
Hold on a second here.
Is the VIP in the VIP room...

141
00:08:21,968 --> 00:08:23,336
I'm sorry about that.

142
00:08:23,903 --> 00:08:27,006
I'll make sure you don't meet
any other patients from now on.

143
00:08:28,341 --> 00:08:30,843
Are you sure your security is
good enough to keep outsiders out?

144
00:08:30,910 --> 00:08:33,880
If the tabloids find out
I'm hospitalized...

145
00:08:34,747 --> 00:08:36,148
I couldn't stand it.

146
00:08:36,215 --> 00:08:38,784
We're being very prudent,
so don't you worry.

147
00:08:39,318 --> 00:08:41,120
The test results are good.

148
00:08:41,420 --> 00:08:43,189
As planned, we'll operate tomorrow.

149
00:08:43,789 --> 00:08:47,126
With me operating, this simple
surgery will take only 15 minutes.

150
00:08:48,160 --> 00:08:50,329
My schedule is packed.

151
00:08:50,963 --> 00:08:54,200
Get me out of this hospital
as soon as you can.

152
00:08:55,601 --> 00:08:56,636
I will.

153
00:08:56,702 --> 00:09:01,707
Doctor, are you sure you're okay
with Kudo being in this room?

154
00:09:03,042 --> 00:09:05,344
I'll tell them to hand over the VIP room!

155
00:09:08,180 --> 00:09:09,949
- Oh, Dr. Daimon!
- What?

156
00:09:10,249 --> 00:09:14,086
- Doctor! This room is just fine.
- What?

157
00:09:14,587 --> 00:09:17,757
- He's better selling than us.
- Maybe so, but...

158
00:09:17,924 --> 00:09:19,792
Who said you could come in?

159
00:09:20,927 --> 00:09:22,728
Enough! Stop! No!

160
00:09:23,062 --> 00:09:26,799
Even now, I can't sell CDs.

161
00:09:26,999 --> 00:09:29,235
There's no way
he's better selling than me.

162
00:09:29,602 --> 00:09:33,205
The number of times he's been played
on the Internet is amazing!

163
00:09:33,306 --> 00:09:35,241
You can't trust the Internet.

164
00:09:35,308 --> 00:09:37,843
At any rate, he's making more money.

165
00:09:37,944 --> 00:09:40,680
Ma'am, I don't think
that's the issue here.

166
00:09:40,880 --> 00:09:44,050
Yu, you see, he has no money.

167
00:09:45,651 --> 00:09:49,589
Every year, he makes a big show
of doing a charity concert

168
00:09:49,689 --> 00:09:52,692
and spends gobs of money
on it out of his own pocket!

169
00:09:52,825 --> 00:09:55,995
You spend a ton on your car
and your clothes too, right?

170
00:09:56,996 --> 00:09:58,864
He's hardly "great"!

171
00:09:59,332 --> 00:10:00,866
He's strapped for cash.

172
00:10:06,005 --> 00:10:08,207
Money comes and money goes.

173
00:10:08,274 --> 00:10:10,409
It's a man's job to act totally cool

174
00:10:11,010 --> 00:10:12,845
and give people dreams, right?

175
00:10:12,912 --> 00:10:18,951
I'm not paying for the cost of
a bed in a VIP room.

176
00:10:19,986 --> 00:10:21,220
Kyoko...

177
00:10:24,490 --> 00:10:28,194
Fine! I'll let that kid have the VIP room.

178
00:10:28,461 --> 00:10:31,063
Wherever you are, Mr. Kudo, is a VIP room!

179
00:10:31,163 --> 00:10:36,168
Doctor, do you know what it is
I've got that he doesn't?

180
00:10:37,003 --> 00:10:40,006
The pride of being number one.

181
00:10:42,608 --> 00:10:44,944
The pride of being number one.

182
00:10:45,511 --> 00:10:47,980
I'll do things in my own way.

183
00:10:48,648 --> 00:10:51,384
Call the media and have
a press conference.

184
00:10:51,484 --> 00:10:52,485
A press conference?

185
00:10:52,585 --> 00:10:56,989
Get me that person,
the confident female Yuji Kudo.

186
00:10:58,491 --> 00:11:00,226
- You called?
- You were eavesdropping.

187
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:03,829
I'm the good and fast Michiko Daimon.

188
00:11:03,996 --> 00:11:07,566
You really are fast.
I'm liking you more all the time.

189
00:11:08,601 --> 00:11:10,202
Big news!

190
00:11:11,804 --> 00:11:13,105
- Big news!
- Okay.

191
00:11:13,305 --> 00:11:16,909
Tomorrow, Yu is going to
hold a press conference.

192
00:11:17,009 --> 00:11:20,279
- Yu?
- Oh, Yuji Kudo.

193
00:11:20,346 --> 00:11:23,549
I happened to be passing by
his room and heard them talking.

194
00:11:23,649 --> 00:11:25,518
- "Happened to"?
- That's good news.

195
00:11:25,685 --> 00:11:27,219
This will be a rocking press conference.

196
00:11:27,319 --> 00:11:28,387
That's right!

197
00:11:29,822 --> 00:11:34,160
What? Ebina would usually
come rushing in at a time like this.

198
00:11:34,260 --> 00:11:35,461
Where is he?

199
00:11:35,795 --> 00:11:38,030
He's using up his vacation days
this whole week.

200
00:11:38,264 --> 00:11:42,668
Due to labor reforms,
the plebes are forced to take vacations.

201
00:11:43,102 --> 00:11:48,040
Those aren't labor reforms.
They're more like no-labor reforms.

202
00:11:48,107 --> 00:11:49,742
What?

203
00:11:50,409 --> 00:11:52,378
You're not letting me do the surgery?

204
00:11:52,445 --> 00:11:53,713
I'm doing the surgery.

205
00:11:54,547 --> 00:11:56,015
I want you

206
00:11:56,582 --> 00:11:59,518
to think of a disease name
appropriate for me

207
00:11:59,652 --> 00:12:01,520
and be at the press conference.

208
00:12:02,388 --> 00:12:04,156
All you've got are hemorrhoids.

209
00:12:04,990 --> 00:12:06,225
How did you know?

210
00:12:07,193 --> 00:12:08,360
I didn't say a word.

211
00:12:08,427 --> 00:12:10,996
I didn't have to ask. There's that.

212
00:12:11,130 --> 00:12:13,599
At any rate, you do the surgery,

213
00:12:13,666 --> 00:12:16,469
you do the press conference.
I appreciate it.

214
00:12:16,535 --> 00:12:18,237
- I'd be honored!
- I decline.

215
00:12:19,438 --> 00:12:22,274
You mean you're rejecting
a request from Kudo?

216
00:12:25,010 --> 00:12:27,880
There are no cool diseases
or uncool diseases.

217
00:12:28,914 --> 00:12:32,885
There are diseases that can be cured
and those that can't.

218
00:12:32,952 --> 00:12:36,222
That's your view of the world,
but I'm Yuji Kudo.

219
00:12:37,089 --> 00:12:40,426
The only thing that matters to me
is if it's cool or not.

220
00:12:42,261 --> 00:12:46,265
<i>Wander free tomorrow, rock 'n' roll heart</i>

221
00:12:48,234 --> 00:12:52,404
<i>Impossible dreams, rock 'n' roll heart</i>

222
00:13:10,222 --> 00:13:11,891
Yes!

223
00:13:13,058 --> 00:13:14,660
See you at the press conference!

224
00:13:26,105 --> 00:13:28,140
Ms. Daimon, what are you watching?

225
00:13:28,407 --> 00:13:30,609
Oh, it's Yu. He's in the hospital, right?

226
00:13:30,676 --> 00:13:32,211
Yes. I saw him in person.

227
00:13:32,645 --> 00:13:35,080
No way! No wonder you're into him now!

228
00:13:35,147 --> 00:13:36,515
No. Don't be stupid.

229
00:13:36,582 --> 00:13:40,619
Michiko, just don't get involved
in a sex scandal with a rock star.

230
00:13:40,719 --> 00:13:43,489
- Say, how old is Yu now?
- Sixty-nine.

231
00:13:43,556 --> 00:13:47,993
But he's sexy and powerful,
and his lifestyle is so cool!

232
00:13:48,060 --> 00:13:50,763
- What kind of lifestyle is that?
- This kind.

233
00:13:50,830 --> 00:13:52,598
Okay. You've got this too.

234
00:13:52,665 --> 00:13:54,433
"<i>Working Your Way Up.</i>

235
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:56,435
I myself am rock 'n' roll."

236
00:13:56,502 --> 00:14:00,406
Since Yu was young, he never
flattered anyone or had groupies.

237
00:14:00,472 --> 00:14:03,909
He climbed his way up alone
with his rock 'n' roll attitude.

238
00:14:04,710 --> 00:14:07,446
He seems a lot like someone I know.

239
00:14:07,513 --> 00:14:09,982
But I can do as good as him.

240
00:14:10,249 --> 00:14:11,417
Rock 'n' roll!

241
00:14:12,618 --> 00:14:14,153
There!

242
00:14:14,220 --> 00:14:15,888
You're looking cool, Akira.

243
00:14:21,193 --> 00:14:23,796
Are you all right, Akira?
Did you throw out your back?

244
00:14:23,863 --> 00:14:25,865
- I knew I couldn't do it.
- You've done it now.

245
00:14:25,965 --> 00:14:28,000
Why were you swinging around a mop?

246
00:14:39,845 --> 00:14:41,146
Dr. Daimon?

247
00:14:42,081 --> 00:14:46,719
Oh, you've decided to be at
my press conference. See you there.

248
00:14:46,785 --> 00:14:47,920
Answer my questions.

249
00:14:48,354 --> 00:14:51,724
Have you experienced
stomach pain or nausea recently?

250
00:14:51,991 --> 00:14:54,393
- Nausea?
- Answer.

251
00:14:56,195 --> 00:14:57,263
Next question.

252
00:14:57,630 --> 00:14:59,431
When you're performing...

253
00:15:00,966 --> 00:15:02,268
Why do you stop here?

254
00:15:04,003 --> 00:15:06,372
Is it because you get intense pain
in your back

255
00:15:06,872 --> 00:15:08,540
and can't move for a moment?

256
00:15:11,410 --> 00:15:14,346
That's the trouble with amateurs.

257
00:15:14,680 --> 00:15:17,850
- That's a break.
- A break?

258
00:15:18,751 --> 00:15:22,521
You take a momentary pause,
then strike your big finish!

259
00:15:22,888 --> 00:15:25,391
Then the fans go wild.

260
00:15:25,491 --> 00:15:27,993
But until a year ago, you went...

261
00:15:30,229 --> 00:15:31,864
There was no break, was there?

262
00:15:33,465 --> 00:15:37,770
Lately, the pain has become worse,
and you can't control your moves.

263
00:15:39,471 --> 00:15:40,839
If I say it doesn't hurt, it doesn't.

264
00:15:40,906 --> 00:15:42,341
Don't treat me like an old man.

265
00:15:42,508 --> 00:15:46,211
I'm only here for
an operation for hemorrhoids.

266
00:15:46,278 --> 00:15:48,180
This could be a disease
worse than hemorrhoids.

267
00:15:51,283 --> 00:15:54,286
What is this disease
that's worse than hemorrhoids?

268
00:15:54,353 --> 00:15:57,756
Let's get you tested right away.
If we don't hurry, it will be too late.

269
00:15:57,923 --> 00:16:00,359
- Yu--
- Butt out of this.

270
00:16:02,161 --> 00:16:04,430
I've got a press conference now.

271
00:16:04,496 --> 00:16:07,166
This is no time for a press conference.

272
00:16:12,638 --> 00:16:16,008
Good morning.
Many people from the media are here.

273
00:16:16,108 --> 00:16:17,443
Is that right?

274
00:16:17,543 --> 00:16:19,945
Let's get you tested.

275
00:16:20,512 --> 00:16:22,014
Dr. Daimon, what's the matter?

276
00:16:22,081 --> 00:16:25,117
I think this doctor is a little crazy.

277
00:16:27,086 --> 00:16:28,687
- Bring that.
- Yes, sir.

278
00:16:28,954 --> 00:16:31,223
This is a race against time.

279
00:16:32,992 --> 00:16:34,560
YUJI KUDO

280
00:16:35,527 --> 00:16:36,462
Here we go.

281
00:16:38,130 --> 00:16:39,565
Oh, Yu!

282
00:16:56,148 --> 00:16:58,584
Nice to meet you. I'm Yuji Kudo.

283
00:17:01,687 --> 00:17:03,122
Please, have a seat.

284
00:17:03,222 --> 00:17:05,591
Thank you all for coming.

285
00:17:05,691 --> 00:17:09,795
I'd like to now inform you about
the treatment for

286
00:17:09,928 --> 00:17:12,731
the big star, Yuji Kudo.

287
00:17:14,366 --> 00:17:16,568
I am Dr. Hideki Kaji,
director of Next-Generation

288
00:17:16,635 --> 00:17:18,203
Ultra-Minimally Invasive Surgery.

289
00:17:19,405 --> 00:17:21,306
I am the surgeon Mamoru Hara.

290
00:17:21,407 --> 00:17:25,010
I will explain the surgery
we will perform.

291
00:17:25,144 --> 00:17:29,281
Mr. Kudo's disease is called
Dockelburn Syndrome.

292
00:17:29,548 --> 00:17:33,819
That's what the tests show,
but don't you worry.

293
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:40,592
No way. It wasn't just hemorrhoids?

294
00:17:41,660 --> 00:17:42,895
It's just hemorrhoids.

295
00:17:43,595 --> 00:17:45,998
Most likely, that's a made-up name.

296
00:17:46,932 --> 00:17:49,501
It's time.
Please come to the operating room.

297
00:17:50,069 --> 00:17:53,105
Again this year, Yuji Kudo plans on having

298
00:17:53,205 --> 00:17:55,941
an enormous charity concert at year's end.

299
00:17:56,075 --> 00:17:58,243
I promise you that this will be

300
00:17:58,343 --> 00:18:03,782
a perfect surgery,
and he will make a full recovery.

301
00:18:03,916 --> 00:18:06,351
We will do our utmost. Thank you.

302
00:18:06,718 --> 00:18:08,620
Thank you, doctors.

303
00:18:09,721 --> 00:18:11,223
Let's all do our best.

304
00:18:11,423 --> 00:18:12,791
Yes, let's do our best.

305
00:18:13,325 --> 00:18:14,193
Okay.

306
00:18:16,995 --> 00:18:18,530
Go ahead. What?

307
00:18:20,799 --> 00:18:22,201
- Are you okay?
- Don't move!

308
00:18:22,634 --> 00:18:24,403
It's okay. It's nothing.

309
00:18:27,873 --> 00:18:29,007
Yu!

310
00:18:29,408 --> 00:18:30,809
- Stretcher!
- Right!

311
00:18:44,156 --> 00:18:45,557
Oh, dear...

312
00:18:53,265 --> 00:18:54,500
My

313
00:18:56,235 --> 00:18:58,036
worst suspicions were right.

314
00:19:01,073 --> 00:19:02,374
Yu...

315
00:19:12,117 --> 00:19:13,519
I need to speak with you.

316
00:19:15,387 --> 00:19:18,290
Is it good news? Or is it bad news?

317
00:19:20,559 --> 00:19:22,060
It's the test results.

318
00:19:24,196 --> 00:19:26,431
It sounds like
I don't just have hemorrhoids.

319
00:19:27,833 --> 00:19:30,235
We found that you have
retroperitoneal sarcoma.

320
00:19:30,302 --> 00:19:31,803
Sarcoma?

321
00:19:33,672 --> 00:19:35,007
That's cancer, right?

322
00:19:37,142 --> 00:19:40,879
It can be cured with surgery, right?

323
00:19:44,316 --> 00:19:45,517
You know,

324
00:19:45,918 --> 00:19:49,788
why don't you just snip that out
when you do my hemorrhoid surgery?

325
00:19:51,690 --> 00:19:53,125
Can't you

326
00:19:54,226 --> 00:19:55,827
operate on it?

327
00:20:03,468 --> 00:20:06,505
I'm not going to die, right, Doctor?

328
00:20:07,472 --> 00:20:09,241
I'm Yuji Kudo.

329
00:20:11,543 --> 00:20:15,180
I can't let cancer get the best of me,
understand?

330
00:20:17,849 --> 00:20:20,152
We will do our best.

331
00:20:33,665 --> 00:20:37,836
What? Yuji Kudo doesn't have hemorrhoids?

332
00:20:37,970 --> 00:20:39,104
Right.

333
00:20:42,040 --> 00:20:43,942
Yuji Kudo, age 69.

334
00:20:44,109 --> 00:20:47,779
He's been diagnosed with
stage three retroperitoneal sarcoma.

335
00:20:49,314 --> 00:20:52,117
There is a 15-centimeter tumor
around the abdominal aorta

336
00:20:52,251 --> 00:20:54,119
near the origin of the celiac artery.

337
00:20:54,186 --> 00:20:55,687
Oh, my goodness.

338
00:20:55,754 --> 00:20:57,189
You must be kidding.

339
00:20:57,589 --> 00:21:00,726
The abdominal aorta is
surrounded by the tumor.

340
00:21:01,994 --> 00:21:05,197
It's enormous. It must be 16 centimeters.

341
00:21:05,364 --> 00:21:08,800
Dr. Hara.
What in the world is going on here?

342
00:21:08,867 --> 00:21:10,068
I'm terribly sorry.

343
00:21:10,602 --> 00:21:13,772
You were so focused on
the hemorrhoid surgery

344
00:21:14,039 --> 00:21:16,475
that you didn't see a sarcoma this large?

345
00:21:16,875 --> 00:21:19,144
I am truly very sorry.

346
00:21:19,678 --> 00:21:21,647
Retroperitoneal sarcoma
is a silent killer.

347
00:21:22,047 --> 00:21:23,949
The patient doesn't have any symptoms,

348
00:21:24,016 --> 00:21:26,585
so it's no surprise it wasn't found
in pre-op tests.

349
00:21:28,453 --> 00:21:29,721
Hey!

350
00:21:30,055 --> 00:21:33,392
Ms. Daimon, why are you so silent?

351
00:21:34,760 --> 00:21:38,363
You're always talking big
and saying, "Let me operate!"

352
00:21:38,597 --> 00:21:40,232
or "I can do this surgery!"

353
00:21:45,537 --> 00:21:48,707
Early symptoms are abdominal pain, nausea,

354
00:21:49,374 --> 00:21:50,676
and anemia.

355
00:21:53,145 --> 00:21:56,548
Eventually, there are
bouts of intense pain.

356
00:22:03,989 --> 00:22:06,458
Stage three retroperitoneal sarcoma.

357
00:22:08,026 --> 00:22:09,428
I had the same.

358
00:22:10,796 --> 00:22:11,630
Really?

359
00:22:11,697 --> 00:22:15,967
But you're alive,
and you're doing just fine.

360
00:22:16,034 --> 00:22:19,171
When you had your surgery
back then, Daimon,

361
00:22:20,405 --> 00:22:23,241
it was Dr. Kaji and Dr. Hara
who performed it, right?

362
00:22:24,242 --> 00:22:26,244
Won't it be all right this time too?

363
00:22:28,046 --> 00:22:29,381
Dr. Daimon,

364
00:22:30,382 --> 00:22:31,883
now's the time

365
00:22:32,317 --> 00:22:35,787
when you should be saying,
"I never fail," right?

366
00:22:42,527 --> 00:22:43,962
In my case,

367
00:22:45,397 --> 00:22:47,299
the tumor wasn't this large.

368
00:22:47,966 --> 00:22:49,568
This will probably be

369
00:22:49,668 --> 00:22:51,803
a more formidable surgery than that one.

370
00:22:53,271 --> 00:22:57,676
You must be kidding me.
I can't believe this.

371
00:22:58,076 --> 00:23:02,314
I made a promise
during that press conference.

372
00:23:02,781 --> 00:23:05,784
Don't you know what kind of
situation this puts me in?

373
00:23:05,851 --> 00:23:07,519
Who cares about that?

374
00:23:07,953 --> 00:23:09,588
If we allow Yu to die,

375
00:23:10,322 --> 00:23:12,290
his fans nationwide won't stand for it!

376
00:23:19,030 --> 00:23:22,901
Excuse me! There's trouble!
Yuji Kudo has disappeared!

377
00:23:23,001 --> 00:23:24,836
I can't find him anywhere.

378
00:23:32,711 --> 00:23:33,879
Dr. Hara!

379
00:23:34,079 --> 00:23:35,614
- Was he on the second floor?
- No, he wasn't.

380
00:23:35,680 --> 00:23:37,215
Check the first floor.
I'll check the third.

381
00:23:37,282 --> 00:23:38,316
Okay. Thank you.

382
00:23:58,069 --> 00:23:59,237
Yu...

383
00:24:03,074 --> 00:24:04,209
Excuse me.

384
00:24:04,709 --> 00:24:06,745
Have you seen Yu?

385
00:24:06,978 --> 00:24:09,047
No, I haven't seen him.

386
00:24:09,281 --> 00:24:10,649
Come on, Dr. Kaji!

387
00:24:12,684 --> 00:24:13,919
Wait!

388
00:24:20,759 --> 00:24:23,061
I think this looks like Yu's motorcycle.

389
00:24:23,462 --> 00:24:25,664
Let's look around in this area.

390
00:24:33,071 --> 00:24:34,206
Yu...

391
00:24:34,673 --> 00:24:38,276
I don't know what to do now!

392
00:24:39,211 --> 00:24:40,412
Yu...

393
00:24:42,247 --> 00:24:43,348
Yu!

394
00:24:52,924 --> 00:24:53,992
<i>I can't take this.</i>

395
00:24:55,126 --> 00:24:59,364
I can't even operate on
my most precious pupil.

396
00:25:00,232 --> 00:25:01,633
I don't know why...

397
00:25:03,001 --> 00:25:04,269
I don't know why

398
00:25:04,970 --> 00:25:07,305
I ever became a doctor.

399
00:25:08,440 --> 00:25:11,510
<i>I want you to</i>

400
00:25:12,010 --> 00:25:13,778
<i>live so much longer.</i>

401
00:25:28,994 --> 00:25:31,396
ODEN

402
00:25:35,834 --> 00:25:39,404
I never thought you'd actually come, Yu.

403
00:25:39,604 --> 00:25:42,140
I'll look after your motorcycle tonight.

404
00:25:42,274 --> 00:25:43,375
Thanks, man.

405
00:25:44,276 --> 00:25:47,112
I wanted to ride farther on my bike.

406
00:25:47,178 --> 00:25:50,916
But your butt hurt,
so you couldn't ride, right?

407
00:25:51,249 --> 00:25:54,286
- What a bother you are.
- You're a Yu groupie?

408
00:25:56,688 --> 00:26:00,025
I've been looking all over for you.
I'm starving.

409
00:26:00,692 --> 00:26:03,862
Sir, I'll have hot sake and <i>oden</i> too.

410
00:26:03,962 --> 00:26:05,530
Okay. Coming right up.

411
00:26:06,932 --> 00:26:08,967
I'll keep watch to keep away the weirdos.

412
00:26:19,644 --> 00:26:23,515
Far away? Where did you plan on going?

413
00:26:26,351 --> 00:26:28,086
To an old friend's place?

414
00:26:30,989 --> 00:26:32,490
I thought about it,

415
00:26:33,925 --> 00:26:35,760
but I don't have any friends.

416
00:26:35,827 --> 00:26:37,162
ODEN

417
00:26:37,228 --> 00:26:39,531
I've lived my life as a lone wolf.

418
00:26:41,266 --> 00:26:43,902
I never let anyone get close to me.

419
00:26:45,704 --> 00:26:49,641
I had never once
given a single thought to dying.

420
00:26:52,277 --> 00:26:55,313
I'm still living my dream.

421
00:26:56,848 --> 00:26:58,316
I don't want to die!

422
00:26:59,884 --> 00:27:01,820
I'm afraid of dying!

423
00:27:10,028 --> 00:27:11,396
What are

424
00:27:12,464 --> 00:27:14,165
the chances I can be saved?

425
00:27:15,867 --> 00:27:17,268
Tell me honestly.

426
00:27:19,971 --> 00:27:21,973
It's a brutal surgery, right?

427
00:27:32,851 --> 00:27:34,285
Okay, I'll tell you.

428
00:27:36,621 --> 00:27:38,023
It's 50-50.

429
00:27:40,625 --> 00:27:41,926
Or

430
00:27:43,728 --> 00:27:45,096
even less.

431
00:27:49,634 --> 00:27:52,604
If you don't get surgery,
you can sing for three more months.

432
00:27:54,506 --> 00:27:58,643
But the disease will progress
during that time,

433
00:28:02,113 --> 00:28:04,482
and there's a 100 percent chance
you'll die.

434
00:28:14,526 --> 00:28:17,195
So 50-50 or even less?

435
00:28:18,863 --> 00:28:20,365
You must be kidding me.

436
00:28:21,966 --> 00:28:23,334
This is ridiculous!

437
00:28:25,870 --> 00:28:28,073
You can say that because you're a doctor.

438
00:28:28,907 --> 00:28:30,875
Put yourself in the patient's shoes!

439
00:28:32,010 --> 00:28:33,378
Who the heck

440
00:28:35,647 --> 00:28:37,549
would let someone do surgery like that?

441
00:28:40,285 --> 00:28:41,686
Get away from me!

442
00:28:42,053 --> 00:28:43,455
Go away!

443
00:28:46,357 --> 00:28:48,727
I want to save you!

444
00:28:51,863 --> 00:28:54,132
Everyone is afraid of dying.

445
00:28:56,901 --> 00:28:58,870
I was afraid too.

446
00:29:13,485 --> 00:29:15,487
Retroperitoneal sarcoma,

447
00:29:16,688 --> 00:29:18,256
stage three.

448
00:29:19,557 --> 00:29:21,559
I had the same disease.

449
00:29:25,864 --> 00:29:27,232
Naturally,

450
00:29:28,833 --> 00:29:31,569
I can't operate on my own disease.

451
00:29:32,637 --> 00:29:35,406
I wrote out lots of notes
on the surgical procedure.

452
00:29:36,441 --> 00:29:37,942
I wrote tons of notes!

453
00:29:40,044 --> 00:29:41,579
And entrusted myself to them.

454
00:29:43,515 --> 00:29:45,416
Did they save you?

455
00:29:51,189 --> 00:29:52,457
That's why

456
00:29:55,393 --> 00:29:57,028
I will,

457
00:30:00,632 --> 00:30:02,100
with these hands,

458
00:30:03,902 --> 00:30:05,136
save you.

459
00:30:19,384 --> 00:30:20,652
What does it feel like

460
00:30:20,952 --> 00:30:25,023
to cut into a patient's body
with a scalpel?

461
00:30:31,229 --> 00:30:33,431
At first, I was so afraid,
I was trembling.

462
00:30:36,501 --> 00:30:38,503
A physician can never make a mistake.

463
00:30:41,239 --> 00:30:42,740
So, I told myself

464
00:30:44,709 --> 00:30:47,011
I never fail.

465
00:30:48,046 --> 00:30:49,547
I said it out loud.

466
00:30:50,782 --> 00:30:53,051
Unless I conquer myself like that,

467
00:30:54,619 --> 00:30:56,621
I can't save my patients.

468
00:31:06,464 --> 00:31:07,699
We're alike.

469
00:31:11,302 --> 00:31:13,938
You are just barely conquering too.

470
00:31:18,309 --> 00:31:19,944
Can you conquer

471
00:31:22,580 --> 00:31:23,781
my surgery too?

472
00:31:34,525 --> 00:31:35,727
I swear

473
00:31:37,328 --> 00:31:38,596
I'll conquer.

474
00:31:39,631 --> 00:31:41,065
Dr. Daimon.

475
00:31:44,402 --> 00:31:45,637
I'm counting on you.

476
00:31:47,939 --> 00:31:49,340
I'm depending on you!

477
00:32:02,954 --> 00:32:04,355
I...

478
00:32:05,223 --> 00:32:07,091
never fail.

479
00:32:08,326 --> 00:32:09,627
You just watch.

480
00:32:38,122 --> 00:32:39,490
It'll be fine, Daimon.

481
00:32:39,557 --> 00:32:42,660
Hara, Jonouchi, and I have
already done this successfully.

482
00:32:42,994 --> 00:32:46,264
So the fact that you can
operate like this is

483
00:32:46,431 --> 00:32:48,199
thanks to us. Take that!

484
00:32:51,436 --> 00:32:53,271
- Let's go.
- Yes, ma'am.

485
00:32:54,072 --> 00:32:57,141
First, we'll ablate the tumor
from the liver and pancreas.

486
00:32:57,275 --> 00:32:59,477
Then we'll check the kidneys and aorta

487
00:32:59,544 --> 00:33:01,079
and ablate it from the celiac artery.

488
00:33:01,145 --> 00:33:03,848
Dr. Kaji and I will follow up
by focusing on the arteries.

489
00:33:04,882 --> 00:33:05,984
Let's get started.

490
00:33:06,084 --> 00:33:09,721
We will now begin the excision of
Yuji Kudo's retroperitoneal sarcoma.

491
00:33:09,787 --> 00:33:10,922
Let's begin.

492
00:33:10,989 --> 00:33:14,859
BP, 117 over 82. Pulse, 84, sinus.

493
00:33:14,993 --> 00:33:16,127
- Scalpel.
- Here.

494
00:33:33,644 --> 00:33:35,346
Don't trouble yourselves over me.

495
00:33:35,480 --> 00:33:39,250
I'm only here as a representative
of Yu's fans nationwide.

496
00:33:43,421 --> 00:33:46,557
If you mess up,
I won't take any responsibility.

497
00:33:52,063 --> 00:33:55,500
Hepatic portal exposed.
Next, I'll clear around the pancreas.

498
00:33:55,600 --> 00:33:58,169
- All right. Retractor.
- Here.

499
00:34:15,153 --> 00:34:16,020
Oh, dear!

500
00:34:16,120 --> 00:34:18,723
The tumor's adhesion
to the aorta is too strong.

501
00:34:18,823 --> 00:34:21,192
There's invasive adhesion
on the left kidney too.

502
00:34:21,292 --> 00:34:24,929
How are we supposed to remove it?
We'll never ablate the tumor now.

503
00:34:26,063 --> 00:34:28,499
- Dr. Daimon!
- Ms. Daimon.

504
00:34:37,275 --> 00:34:39,811
- Change in surgical procedure.
- Change in surgical procedure?

505
00:34:39,877 --> 00:34:43,514
Total tumor removal via combined
resection of the left kidney and aorta.

506
00:34:43,681 --> 00:34:45,750
Then we'll replace it with
a synthetic vascular prosthesis.

507
00:34:45,817 --> 00:34:47,018
- Are you crazy?
- That's impossible!

508
00:34:47,085 --> 00:34:48,419
Don't even try it!

509
00:34:50,354 --> 00:34:52,390
- Prep the PCPS.
- Right.

510
00:34:54,826 --> 00:34:55,726
Here.

511
00:34:58,596 --> 00:35:00,631
- Prep the heparinized saline solution.
- Right.

512
00:35:11,008 --> 00:35:13,878
The tumor has infiltrated to
right under the aortic opening.

513
00:35:14,479 --> 00:35:17,115
We can't use a synthetic
vascular prosthesis like this.

514
00:35:19,083 --> 00:35:20,485
It's impossible to do anything else.

515
00:35:21,252 --> 00:35:23,921
It's not impossible.
I'm sure we can overcome this.

516
00:35:26,390 --> 00:35:30,061
It's all right. He has always
just barely conquered things.

517
00:35:31,762 --> 00:35:33,564
What's she talking about?

518
00:35:34,132 --> 00:35:35,366
Michiko...

519
00:35:36,067 --> 00:35:38,269
Let's replace it
with a hybrid synthetic graft.

520
00:35:39,237 --> 00:35:41,005
A hybrid synthetic graft?

521
00:35:41,506 --> 00:35:43,141
We don't have one of those.

522
00:35:46,077 --> 00:35:48,946
- Get that thing immediately.
- Right.

523
00:35:52,183 --> 00:35:54,585
We used it during Dr. Daimon's surgery.

524
00:35:54,652 --> 00:35:56,154
I prepped it.

525
00:35:57,221 --> 00:35:58,222
Thank you.

526
00:35:58,356 --> 00:36:01,859
- Hara, totally awesome job.
- Thanks.

527
00:36:02,760 --> 00:36:03,995
What's that all about?

528
00:36:04,061 --> 00:36:08,266
A hybrid synthetic graft is
a synthetic vascular prosthesis

529
00:36:08,599 --> 00:36:10,601
attached to a stent graft.

530
00:36:11,369 --> 00:36:13,404
Due to the stent's pressure bonding,

531
00:36:14,105 --> 00:36:16,274
you can connect the vessels

532
00:36:16,707 --> 00:36:18,442
without suturing them.

533
00:36:20,044 --> 00:36:23,714
Dr. Hara saved them this once.

534
00:36:26,083 --> 00:36:27,518
I'm back.

535
00:36:28,953 --> 00:36:30,454
This will work.

536
00:36:30,821 --> 00:36:33,758
We'll replace the aorta with
a hybrid synthetic graft.

537
00:36:33,891 --> 00:36:34,825
- Right.
- Yes.

538
00:36:34,926 --> 00:36:36,961
- Exposing the aorta. Metzenbaum.
- Here.

539
00:36:37,061 --> 00:36:39,230
- Widen the view from that side.
- Got it.

540
00:36:40,131 --> 00:36:41,199
Here goes.

541
00:36:54,612 --> 00:36:57,748
SURGERY TIME

542
00:36:58,950 --> 00:37:00,084
What are his vitals?

543
00:37:00,151 --> 00:37:03,988
BP, 109 over 78. Pulse, 77, sinus.

544
00:37:05,156 --> 00:37:07,191
- Good work.
- Well done.

545
00:37:08,793 --> 00:37:10,394
That's Yuji Kudo for you.

546
00:37:10,995 --> 00:37:12,863
He stuck in there and roughed it out.

547
00:37:17,568 --> 00:37:19,937
Dr. Daimon, well done.

548
00:37:22,640 --> 00:37:24,008
Dr. Daimon!

549
00:37:26,344 --> 00:37:27,812
As his attending physician

550
00:37:28,746 --> 00:37:31,782
and a fan of Yu, let me express my thanks.

551
00:37:33,484 --> 00:37:34,785
Thank you.

552
00:37:37,822 --> 00:37:40,024
You can do the hemorrhoid surgery.

553
00:37:40,791 --> 00:37:41,926
Okay!

554
00:37:45,496 --> 00:37:46,597
SHIGEKATSU HIRUMA

555
00:37:46,664 --> 00:37:50,635
Dr. Michiko Daimon's surgeries
sure don't do my heart any good.

556
00:37:51,202 --> 00:37:55,273
Ruri, can you get me
something sweet to eat?

557
00:37:55,506 --> 00:37:58,409
Something sweet, like <i>daifuku.</i>

558
00:37:58,476 --> 00:38:01,879
- Excuse me.
- Get me a <i>daifuku,</i> please.

559
00:38:02,913 --> 00:38:05,816
- Oh, you're already here?
- I don't have any <i>daifuku,</i>

560
00:38:05,883 --> 00:38:07,418
but I do have a melon.

561
00:38:08,052 --> 00:38:09,520
- This is a melon.
- Okay.

562
00:38:12,089 --> 00:38:14,292
- This is the bill.
- Okay.

563
00:38:15,926 --> 00:38:18,763
But the operation just ended.
Isn't this awfully fast?

564
00:38:20,364 --> 00:38:21,899
This is far too expensive.

565
00:38:21,966 --> 00:38:25,703
Naturally, Totei University
will get the credit for the surgery.

566
00:38:26,103 --> 00:38:29,307
The fee for keeping our silence has
also become great.

567
00:38:29,607 --> 00:38:31,208
I appreciate your cooperation.

568
00:38:34,145 --> 00:38:36,347
This feels great!

569
00:38:36,981 --> 00:38:39,150
Job well done.

570
00:38:39,383 --> 00:38:42,386
Thank you for saving Yu's life.

571
00:38:43,087 --> 00:38:44,055
What?

572
00:38:44,121 --> 00:38:47,525
Allow me to wash your back
as a token of my thanks.

573
00:38:48,192 --> 00:38:49,860
I never said anything,

574
00:38:49,994 --> 00:38:53,331
but I'm actually a secret fan of Yu!

575
00:38:53,397 --> 00:38:56,000
He's completely different than my husband,

576
00:38:56,167 --> 00:38:59,036
the dentist I met at Totei University.

577
00:38:59,970 --> 00:39:03,874
But you have to promise to
keep this a secret.

578
00:39:05,109 --> 00:39:08,846
Everyone at the hospital already knows.

579
00:39:09,580 --> 00:39:11,982
What? You're kidding!

580
00:39:17,088 --> 00:39:19,090
ALBERT SAVAROTTI

581
00:39:19,156 --> 00:39:23,794
You saw, Ben Casey.
Don't tell a soul. It's a secret.

582
00:39:23,861 --> 00:39:26,230
- I'm back!
- Welcome back.

583
00:39:27,131 --> 00:39:28,766
What are you doing, Akira?

584
00:39:28,833 --> 00:39:32,470
I made all your
favorite foods today, Michiko.

585
00:39:36,707 --> 00:39:38,843
Crab cream croquettes!

586
00:39:39,543 --> 00:39:41,412
What a great smell!

587
00:39:41,645 --> 00:39:44,949
Oh, that's right.
This arrived for you here.

588
00:39:46,550 --> 00:39:47,785
Thank you.

589
00:39:58,362 --> 00:39:59,797
Excuse me.

590
00:40:03,300 --> 00:40:05,836
This is my fifth time, you know.

591
00:40:08,172 --> 00:40:09,573
Why...

592
00:40:10,841 --> 00:40:16,847
why won't my husband
even let me, his wife, see him?

593
00:40:27,558 --> 00:40:32,296
Nichotan! You finally came to see me.

594
00:40:34,999 --> 00:40:36,400
This is my husband.

595
00:40:37,468 --> 00:40:39,904
It's been a while. How have you been?

596
00:40:41,572 --> 00:40:44,041
Why in the world do you keep coming here?

597
00:40:45,075 --> 00:40:47,678
And you even lie
that you're my common-law wife.

598
00:40:50,881 --> 00:40:53,884
Because I want to operate on you.

599
00:40:55,719 --> 00:40:58,422
You have a congenital heart disease.

600
00:40:58,589 --> 00:41:00,991
A congenitally corrected
transposition of the great arteries.

601
00:41:01,926 --> 00:41:04,061
The right and left chambers are reversed.

602
00:41:04,195 --> 00:41:05,496
How did you know that?

603
00:41:16,207 --> 00:41:19,143
With the dangerous condition
your heart is in,

604
00:41:19,944 --> 00:41:21,712
I couldn't just ignore you.

605
00:41:21,979 --> 00:41:23,447
It's none of your business.

606
00:41:24,548 --> 00:41:27,852
- I'm as good as dead.
- You're still alive.

607
00:41:31,755 --> 00:41:34,225
Hurry up and tell them everything
and get out of jail.

608
00:41:36,460 --> 00:41:38,262
With you here, I can't operate on you.

609
00:41:39,163 --> 00:41:40,998
What good would that do?

610
00:41:42,199 --> 00:41:43,834
I don't care if

611
00:41:45,069 --> 00:41:46,604
my heart stopped right now.

612
00:41:47,771 --> 00:41:50,708
However, I'm worried about the future of

613
00:41:51,008 --> 00:41:53,244
this country and its children.

614
00:41:55,579 --> 00:41:58,048
That university hospital
full of weaklings...

615
00:41:58,516 --> 00:42:01,285
In fact, this country itself

616
00:42:02,086 --> 00:42:04,989
will soon be gobbled up
by an enormous black bass.

617
00:42:05,756 --> 00:42:06,824
Hey!

618
00:42:08,759 --> 00:42:10,628
A genius like you

619
00:42:12,396 --> 00:42:13,831
should get out now.

620
00:42:15,232 --> 00:42:18,235
Farewell, my friend.

621
00:42:21,238 --> 00:42:24,275
Hey! Nichotan!

622
00:42:26,710 --> 00:42:30,347
<i>This is the story of
a maverick female doctor.</i>

623
00:42:40,624 --> 00:42:41,959
Hey! Are you all right?

624
00:42:42,326 --> 00:42:46,964
We were able to release you
in time for the charity concert.

625
00:42:47,565 --> 00:42:48,465
Thank you.

626
00:42:49,600 --> 00:42:52,269
There's a patient I'd like to introduce.

627
00:42:54,705 --> 00:42:55,773
Come on.

628
00:43:02,846 --> 00:43:05,382
This is Kazuto Yoshiyuki.

629
00:43:06,317 --> 00:43:09,887
Kazuto is very young,
but he's a genius pianist.

630
00:43:10,321 --> 00:43:13,824
He was going to play with me
during this year's charity concert.

631
00:43:14,491 --> 00:43:17,561
But now he has a serious disease.

632
00:43:17,995 --> 00:43:21,732
At this rate, he may not
be able to keep playing the piano.

633
00:43:22,232 --> 00:43:25,869
But, Kazuto, don't you worry.

634
00:43:26,503 --> 00:43:28,238
Here at Totei University,

635
00:43:29,106 --> 00:43:30,808
there's a magnificent doctor.

636
00:43:30,874 --> 00:43:33,877
That's exactly right.
We have magnificent doctors everywhere.

637
00:43:34,244 --> 00:43:38,315
The doctor who saved me,
Dr. Michiko Daimon.

638
00:43:39,516 --> 00:43:43,621
I entrust Kazuto's life to Dr. Daimon.

639
00:43:44,355 --> 00:43:48,826
Dr. Michiko Daimon is super great!

640
00:43:48,892 --> 00:43:50,828
<i>This woman hates groups,</i>

641
00:43:50,928 --> 00:43:55,199
<i>hates authority, and hates restrictions.</i>

642
00:43:55,499 --> 00:43:58,669
<i>Her specialized medical license
and well-honed skills</i>

643
00:43:58,836 --> 00:44:00,104
<i>are her weapons.</i>

644
00:44:01,572 --> 00:44:02,906
I'll ask you again.

645
00:44:03,440 --> 00:44:06,510
You agree to a plea bargain, right?

646
00:44:07,711 --> 00:44:12,082
Yes. I merely followed his orders.

647
00:44:14,985 --> 00:44:16,453
Everything

648
00:44:17,354 --> 00:44:20,391
was by the direction of Tange Nicholas.

649
00:44:37,141 --> 00:44:38,676
<i>My diagnosis is</i>

650
00:44:38,742 --> 00:44:41,845
<i>congenitally corrected
transposition of the great arteries.</i>

651
00:44:42,179 --> 00:44:44,548
<i>If he suffers cardiac failure,</i>

652
00:44:44,715 --> 00:44:47,985
<i>he will require immediate surgery.</i>

653
00:44:48,585 --> 00:44:51,221
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

654
00:44:51,355 --> 00:44:54,725
<i>otherwise known as Doctor X.</i>

655
00:44:56,927 --> 00:44:58,962
FINAL EPISODE

656
00:44:59,163 --> 00:45:00,831
<i>I want my life to end quietly.</i>

657
00:45:00,898 --> 00:45:01,832
I won't abandon him.

658
00:45:01,899 --> 00:45:05,602
<i>- If you operate, you're a criminal.</i>
- I want you to live.

659
00:45:05,669 --> 00:45:08,806
- Suicide? Are you crazy?
- It's cancer.

660
00:45:08,906 --> 00:45:11,709
I absolutely never fail.
